    takeaway:'Spatial is a language and compiler that makes accelerator control, memories, and tuning parameters explicit, then generates hardware with optimized pipelines and storage.',
    hook:'Four arithmetic lanes are not useful if memory feeds only one.',
    problem:'Turning an algorithm into hardware requires decisions about parallelism, pipelining, and memory access that ordinary software code leaves implicit.',
    analogy:'Opening four checkout lanes helps only if customers can reach all four.',
    before:[['Unroll the work','Create several arithmetic lanes'],['Keep one memory path','Supply one operand per cycle','costly'],['Idle hardware','Parallel units wait for data','costly']],
    after:[['Describe control + memory','Expose accelerator-specific structure'],['Coordinate banking and parallelism','Provide compatible data paths','hot'],['Tune and generate','Explore hardware configurations']],
    beforeCaption:'Compute parallelism can outrun available memory access capacity.',afterCaption:'Banking and buffering must match the access pattern, not just the number of lanes.',
    demoTitle:'Four lanes, how many banks?',demoIntro:'Four lanes need four consecutive array elements in one toy cycle. Each bank serves one read. Compare one bank with four cyclically assigned banks.',
    demoModes:[['one','1 bank'],['four','4 banks']],
    exampleFallback:'One single-read bank needs four cycles for four reads. Four banks holding consecutive elements cyclically can serve those reads in one cycle. A different address pattern can still cause bank conflicts.',
    methods:[['Expose hardware concepts','Describe nested control, explicit memories, and interfaces.'],['Optimize the implementation','Coordinate pipelining, memory banking, buffering, and parallelism.'],['Tune parameters','Explore legal configurations before generating target hardware.']],
    contribution:'A high-level accelerator language with a compiler and design-space tuning that retain hardware-relevant structure.',
    bridge:['Application algorithm','Control + memory abstractions','Generated accelerator'],
    connection:'Use Spatial as a conventional reference when claiming task-to-hardware compilation or automatic design tuning in ABCD.',
    experiment:'Vary loop parallelism and bank count together. Check throughput, bank conflicts, and resource use rather than arithmetic-lane count alone.',
    caution:'The toy assumes conflict-free cyclic banking. Real banking must follow the actual index expressions and memory-port limits.',
    evidence:[['2.9×','Reported average FPGA speedup','Compared with SDAccel on the evaluated applications.'],['42% less','Reported source code','The same study compares code size; this is not a guarantee of lower effort for every workload.']],
    limitation:'The comparison uses selected implementations and a historical toolchain. Portability includes evaluated FPGA targets and the Plasticine CGRA, not every possible accelerator.',
    evidencePage:10,evidenceSections:'§5 · FPGA evaluation, tuning, and portability',sourceSections:[['§3 · Language abstractions',4],['§4 · Compiler',7],['§5 · Evaluation',10]],
    related:'calyx',relatedReason:'Calyx focuses on a reusable intermediate representation for accelerator-generating compilers.'
